From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 07:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] media: meson: vdec: VIFIFO level while the VLD is reset

The MPEG-1/2 multi codec resets the VLD between pictures, and until it
restores the read pointer VLD_MEM_VIFIFO_LEVEL reads as the write
pointer's address. The parser sampled it there, took a 16 MiB VIFIFO for
full, and refused all input for good: a decode stalled at its start,
intermittently, and 720x576 hit it most runs.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
 vdec/vdec_1.c |    4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff -ruN a/vdec/vdec_1.c b/vdec/vdec_1.c
--- a/vdec/vdec_1.c
+++ b/vdec/vdec_1.c
@@ -219,8 +219,10 @@
 static u32 vdec_1_vififo_level(struct amvdec_session *sess)
 {
 	struct amvdec_core *core = sess->core;
+	u32 level = amvdec_read_dos(core, VLD_MEM_VIFIFO_LEVEL);
 
-	return amvdec_read_dos(core, VLD_MEM_VIFIFO_LEVEL);
+	/* a frame-based codec resets the VLD between pictures: RP reads 0 */
+	return level > sess->vififo_size ? 0 : level;
 }
 
 static bool vdec_1_stbuf_pointer_valid(struct amvdec_session *sess, u32 ptr)
